@bingwang-ms About the two CodeQL "wrong number of arguments" alerts: `sai_qos_tests.py` imports from `switch`, and CodeQL resolved these calls against the legacy Python 2 `tests/saitests/switch.py`, where `sai_thrift_read_port_counters(client, port)` takes 2 arguments. PTF runs these tests with `--test-dir saitests/py3`, so the module actually used is `tests/saitests/py3/switch.py`, where the signature is `sai_thrift_read_port_counters(client, asic_type, port)`, and the calls were correct at runtime.

The flagged calls were inside a nested helper function in `QSharedWatermarkTest.runTest`; the other calls in the file are made directly in the test methods and are not flagged. e993c11b9 moves the two reads inline into `runTest`, with no change to the computed values or assertions, so the CodeQL check should pass now.

The same change is applied to the msft-202512 manual cherry-pick, Azure/sonic-mgmt.msft#1507.

